# Vault and note creation

The vault is a curated knowledge base, not an automatic transcript sink. Prefer
updating a durable existing page over creating another note.

Adjust `globs` to your vault path if it is not `~/vault`.

## SessionStart hook (optional)

- A Codex (or similar) SessionStart hook may run `vault/.maintenance/check-due.ps1`
  and inject overdue reminders only.
- The hook must never open Obsidian, create notes, edit the vault, or mark a pass complete.
- Obsidian does not need to be running; the vault is ordinary Markdown on disk.

## When creation is allowed

| Destination | Create or update only when |
|---|---|
| `vault/raw/` | The user explicitly captures/imports source material. Preserve it unchanged. |
| `vault/entities/` | A compile finds durable raw evidence about one concrete person, product, client, company, or tool. |
| `vault/concepts/` | A compile finds a reusable idea supported by raw material. |
| `vault/research/` | A research sweep produces a dated, sourced, expiry-tagged result. |
| `~/.agents/memory/notes/` | `extract-approach` passes its trigger gate; register in `MEMORY.md`. |

Weekly lint repairs contradictions, duplicates, dead links, and stale indexes. Weekly
synthesis updates existing knowledge and creates a page only when a genuinely new
cross-source conclusion exists. Neither pass produces filler to prove it ran.

## Create-vs-update gate

Before creating any compiled page:

1. Search `vault/INDEX.md`, then the matching entity/concept/research directory.
2. If an existing page covers the subject, update it in place.
3. Create a new page only when it has one distinct durable subject and supporting evidence.
4. Add or update its one-line entry in `INDEX.md`.

## Never create notes for

- ordinary coding progress, status summaries, or chat transcripts
- mechanical refactors, routine setup, or standard documented procedures
- failed investigations with no validated conclusion
- generic best practices already present in docs or rules
- speculative ideas without a raw source or explicit user request
- duplicate versions of an existing page

Maintenance completion is recorded only after the pass succeeds (for example
`vault/.maintenance/mark-done.ps1 -Pass <name>` when you use that tooling).
